+## Counts, teaching, and common input grammar
 
-The common prototype input domain is 8..30 rows and columns, 1..3 internal full-zero
-divider rows and columns, section sides at least two cells, zero nuisance cells,
-and nonempty local rows and columns. Each section contains at most three nonzero
-colors with **unique minimum and maximum frequencies**. Absent colors are not
-candidates. Tied extrema are rejected. The validator also admits the original
-single-color sections, although those cannot distinguish the two settings.
+`generate_episode(seed, selection=..., demos=3, queries=1)` supports **2–6 demos
+and 1–4 queries independently**. `sample_inputs` accepts the same count keywords.
+The omitted selection is canonical; `selection=None` chooses once from the seed.
